    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "(a) Find the first four terms of $a_{n}=5n+7$.\n(b) Find the first three terms of $b_{n}=(-1)^{n}(3n+4)$.\n(c) Find $c_{4}$ for $c_{n}=\\frac{n}{3n+2}$.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Substitute the position numbers $1,2,3,4$.\n$a_{1}=5(1)+7=12$\n$a_{2}=5(2)+7=17$\n$a_{3}=5(3)+7=22$\n$a_{4}=5(4)+7=27$\n(b) Substitute each position, including in the power of $-1$.\n$b_{1}=(-1)^{1}(3(1)+4)=-7$\n$b_{2}=(-1)^{2}(3(2)+4)=10$\n$b_{3}=(-1)^{3}(3(3)+4)=-13$\n(c) $c_{4}=\\frac{4}{3(4)+2}$\n$c_{4}=\\frac{4}{14}=\\frac{2}{7}$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "(a) A sequence has $a_{1}=8$ and $a_{n}=2a_{n-1}-3$ for $n\\ge2$. Find the first four terms.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Use each term to find the next.\n$a_{1}=8$\n$a_{2}=2(8)-3=13$\n$a_{3}=2(13)-3=23$\n$a_{4}=2(23)-3=43$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "A sequence has the rule $a_{n}=6n+5$.\n(a) Find its first five terms.\n(b) Describe the term-to-term rule in words and write it using sequence notation.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Substitute the position numbers $1,2,3,4,5$.\n$a_{1}=6(1)+5=11$\n$a_{2}=6(2)+5=17$\n$a_{3}=6(3)+5=23$\n$a_{4}=6(4)+5=29$\n$a_{5}=6(5)+5=35$\n(b) Add $6$ to the previous term.\n$a_{1}=11$, and $a_{n}=a_{n-1}+6$ for $n\\ge2$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Determine whether the given number is a term of each sequence.\n(a) $83$ in $a_{n}=5n+8$\n(b) $122$ in $b_{n}=3n^{2}+2$\n(c) $224$ in $c_{n}=7\\times2^{n-1}$",
        "solution_text": "(a) Put $a_{n}=83$.\n$5n+8=83$\n$5n=75$\n$n=15$\nYes, $83$ is the 15th term.\n(b) Put $b_{n}=122$.\n$3n^{2}+2=122$\n$n^{2}=40$\nSince $6^{2}<40<7^{2}$, there is no positive integer position.\nNo, $122$ is not a term.\n(c) Put $c_{n}=224$.\n$7\\times2^{n-1}=224$\n$2^{n-1}=32=2^{5}$\n$n-1=5$\n$n=6$\nYes, $224$ is the 6th term."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "(a) How many negative terms are in $a_{n}=7n-90$?\n(b) Find the position and value of the first term greater than $100$ in $b_{n}=8n-17$.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Put $a_{n}<0$.\n$7n-90<0$\n$7n<90$\n$n<\\frac{90}{7}$\nThe positive integer positions are $1,2,\\dots,12$, so there are $12$ negative terms.\n(b) Put $b_{n}>100$.\n$8n-17>100$\n$8n>117$\n$n>\\frac{117}{8}$\nThe first integer position is $n=15$.\n$b_{15}=8(15)-17=103$\nPosition $15$, value $103$."
      }
    ],
